cdrskin, the CD burner MusicDeck burns audio CDs with (musicdeck/burn.py), is libburn's:

  libburn 1.5.8, https://files.libburnia-project.org/releases/libburn-1.5.8.tar.gz
  SHA-256 8e24dd99f5b7cafbecf0116d61b619ee89098e20263e6f47c793aaf4a98d6473
  signed by Thomas Schmitt <scdbackup@gmx.net>, key 44BC 9FD0 D688 EB00 7C4D D029 E9CB DFC0 ABC0 A854
  (libburn-1.5.8.tar.gz.sig beside it)

Licence: GPL-2.0-or-later (the tarball's COPYING, here cdrskin.COPYING). bin/<platform>/cdrskin is built
from that tarball, unchanged, by scripts/build_cdrskin.sh (static, musl, with zig); its source is the
tarball above.

On Windows, cdrskin.exe is the same libburn built with libcdio as its way of talking to the drive:

  libcdio 2.4.0, https://github.com/libcdio/libcdio/releases/download/2.4.0/libcdio-2.4.0.tar.bz2
  SHA-256 8e6a305f81e45a78b41ce696d34497cc208d97075469d7304c11a6d44bf006ac

libcdio is GPL-3.0-or-later (cdrskin.libcdio.COPYING), so cdrskin.exe as a whole is GPL-3.0-or-later. It
is built by scripts/build_cdrskin_windows.sh (MSYS2's UCRT64 gcc, static) from both tarballs, unchanged,
plus MusicDeck's backend/cdrskin/windows/ (the POSIX functions MinGW lacks); its source is those.
